// Hand-authored Pine v5 fixture — the "three most-common rewrites in one
// script" scenario. Real community v5 indicators frequently combine:
//
//   * study("…", …)             at the top
//   * plot(…, transp=N)         for the fill layer
//   * iff(cond, a, b)           for conditional overlays
//
// All three rewrite in a single migration pass. Idempotence (each rewrite
// runs only once even if the source contains multiple hits) is asserted
// by the C7 unit tests; this integration fixture exercises the combined
// pipeline for a real-shaped script.
//
// Per PRD §2.1: hand-authored, not copied from TradingView.
//
// Covers: study() → indicator(), transp= stripping (2 hits), iff() → (?:),
// input.int(), ta.rsi(), color.new (leave alone), plot() (multiple).
//@version=5
study("Combined Rewrites", overlay=false)
length = input.int(14, minval=1, title="Length")
val = ta.rsi(close, length)
signal = iff(val > 70, val, iff(val < 30, val, 0))
plot(val, title="rsi", color=color.blue, transp=15)
plot(signal, title="sig", color=color.red, transp=0)
